# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Fan-Shun Meng et al. (2024). A highly transferable and efficient machine learning interatomic potentials study of α -Fe–C binary system.
#   Acta Materialia. doi:10.1016/j.actamat.2024.120408
#
# Version read: submittedVersion (sha256 0ea6995c0713f2c6...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 326 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/meng2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: a Behler-Parrinello neural network potential (n2p2) and a
# Deep Potential (DeePMD-kit 2.2.3) for the alpha-Fe-C binary system trained
# on 32,002 spin-polarised DFT configurations (90/10 split), with training
# and test energy and force RMSEs and the MD cost per atom and step.
# Defect, carbide, dislocation and interface properties are not error
# metrics.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
